_shrunk":0.0101273}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000092295","entrez_id":["7051"],"uniprot":["P22735"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a membrane protein that catalyzes the addition of an alkyl group from an akylamine to a glutamine residue of a protein, forming an alkylglutamine in the protein. This protein alkylation leads to crosslinking of proteins and catenation of polyamines to proteins. This gene contains either one or two copies of a 22 nt repeat unit in its 3' UTR. Mutations in this gene have been associated with autosomal recessive lamellar ichthyosis (LI) and nonbullous congenital ichthyosiform erythroderma (NCIE). [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P22735","text":"Catalyzes the cross-linking of proteins and the conjugation of polyamines to proteins (PubMed:7629111, PubMed:8824274, PubMed:26220141, PubMed:20663883). Responsible for cross-linking epidermal proteins during formation of the stratum corneum (PubMed:26220141). Involved in cell proliferation (PubMed:26220141)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}